meta {
  name: Remove Campaign File (After Commit, 409)
  type: http
  seq: 27
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/platform/mailer-campaigns/{{campaignId}}/files/{{campaignVendorFileId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{platformAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 409 Conflict", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(409);
  });

  test("says why", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().message).to.contain("commit");
  });
}

docs {
  # DELETE /platform/mailer-campaigns/:campaignId/files/:fileId — remove a file

  Takes a vendor file off a campaign that has **not** committed, and reads the
  remaining files again (back to `uploaded`, `previewAttempt` bumped).

  - **Module:** none (`@SkipModule()`)
  - **Permission:** `platform:mailers:write`
  - **Data scope:** none (`@SkipTenant()`, `@SkipBranch()`)

  ## Why this request is the refusal

  The collection reaches this point with a campaign that has committed twice,
  and that is the case worth a standing assertion: once any commit has run, the
  file list is the record of what was imported, and removing a file would not
  remove its rows from `mailers`. The correction is to add a corrected file, or
  an overwrite from a new campaign.

  ## Errors
  - `400 Bad Request` — it is the campaign's last file. Delete the campaign
    instead.
  - `404 Not Found` — no file with that id on this campaign.
  - `409 Conflict` — the campaign is `processing` / `imported` / `superseded`,
    or a commit has run (`commitAttempt > 0`).
}
